  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Carbohydrate molecules have hemiacetal or hemiketal groups can reduces Tollen&#39;s reagent and Fehling&#39;s solution are reducing. All monosaccharides are reducing sugars. If any sugar is having free <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>OH</mi></math> group at anomeric carbon then it will be a reducing sugar.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0073_67306df57200.png\" style=\"width: 416px; height: 240px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
